 "rule_label": "ⓘ how this is checked",
 "rule_text": "Every night at 20:15 ET the names on the 🩳 list, the 🔭 follow-up and the 👀 Watch are read again: the float the chip divides by (Yahoo's, with its read date) beside Massive's free float (its effective date), split-adjusted with the splits on file. A second float dated before the splits on file is not compared until the splits read reaches back to its date. A second dated float (Massive's free float) is read beside Yahoo's and both are in the hover with their dates; when it puts an EXTREME name under the cut the chip adds '⚠️ sources disagree' and the word stays. At most 120 outside reads a night; the rest wait for the next night.",
